# What the shipped image copies from app/ and alembic/ is an allowlist by file name and type: a file
# ships when a `!` pattern below names its type and place, wherever it is and whatever its directory
# is called (`app/.aws/c.py` ships; `app/.aws/c.txt` does not). A directory whose own name matches a
# pattern (`app/foo.py/`) lets everything inside it through. tests/test_dockerignore.py matches every
# file and directory under app/ and alembic/ against these patterns as BuildKit does: it fails on a
# file that does not ship (the change_logs and release_notes .md files excepted), since a file left
# out only goes missing at run time, and on a directory named like an allowed type.
app/**
!app/**/*.py
!app/templates/**/*.html
!app/templates/**/*.svg
!app/static/**/*.css
!app/static/**/*.js
alembic/**
!alembic/**/*.py
!alembic/script.py.mako

**/.git
.gitignore
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.Python
env
venv
.venv
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt
.coverage
.tox
.cache
nosetests.xml
coverage.xml
*.cover
**/*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
.claude/
*.swp
*.swo
**/*~
test.db

# Secrets, private topology and data stay out of the rest of the build context, which reaches the css
# stage's layers (luxarch --doc FLEET-BUILD-DEPLOY-STANDARD, "Clean-clone build readiness").
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/*credentials.json
**/service-account*.json
**/secrets.json
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/.netrc
**/.npmrc
**/.pypirc
**/.aws/
**/.ssh/
!.env.example
**/Makefile.local
deploy/
backups/
**/*.sql
**/*.sql.gz
**/*.dump
**/node_modules/
